<title>USA: Midland unit sees $5.2 mln hurricane loss.</title>
<headline>Midland unit sees $5.2 mln hurricane loss.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Modern Insurance Group, a wholly owned subsidiary of Midland Co, estimates its losses from Hurricane Fran will be about $5.2 million after tax, the company said Friday.  </p>
<p>Midland said its subsidiary's losses, net of reinsurance recoveries, would reduce its own third-quarter results by about $1.70 per share after taxes.</p>
<p>It said the losses would likely cause a loss for its consolidated operations in the same period.</p>
</text>
